# /etc/synguard/netwatch-exempt — programs netwatch does not raise alerts for.
#
# netwatch watches each process's outbound connect()s for the shapes a worm
# makes: a subnet sweep, a port scan (many hosts on non-web ports), a connect
# flood. A few legitimate programs make those shapes by design. This file lists
# them by the absolute path of their executable, one per line; `#` starts a
# comment. The connections are still recorded and still go through the rules —
# only netwatch's alert is dropped, and synguard logs that it was.
#
# The path is checked against /proc/<pid>/exe, never against the process name,
# which any program can set to anything. Edits take effect on
# `systemctl reload synguard` (SIGHUP).

# Syncthing's relay pool connects to dozens of relays on 22067/22070 to measure
# them, which reads as a port scan once per boot.
/usr/bin/syncthing
